  "narrative": "I assessed the 12 new discovery results using the pre-specified clinical-support rule: for these negative-valued dependency scores, a 10% clinical benchmark was taken as 10% of the absolute outcome mean, giving benchmarks of about 0.0093 for outcome_014, 0.0269 for outcome_013, 0.0415 for outcome_001, 0.0301 for outcome_011, and 0.0282 for outcome_008. Acceptance requires the signed 95% interval lower bound to reach the outcome-specific benchmark; zero exclusion or a point estimate above benchmark alone is not enough. All reported estimates are already signed to the claim direction, so positive signed values are the ones that support the claimed direction.\n\nFeature_063 coherence: H227 compares outcome_014 feature_063 level_003 versus level_002 in the claimed positive direction. The signed estimate is 0.0214, above the outcome_014 benchmark, but the interval is extremely wide (about -0.0589 to 0.1018) with only 98 observations in the level_003 cell. This is directionally consistent with a level-ordering interpretation of H114, but it is far too imprecise to support or refute anything on its own. I therefore mark H227 unresolved and closed as a standalone test; the broader feature_063 question remains open only through H114. The other coherence claims are less supportive: H133 on outcome_013 has signed estimate -0.0029 with upper bound 0.0182, below the 0.0269 benchmark and opposite the claimed direction, so it is rejected as no clinically meaningful positive association. H222 on outcome_011 has signed estimate 0.0028 and upper bound 0.0274, below the 0.0301 benchmark, and is rejected. H134 on outcome_001 is a near-boundary case: signed estimate 0.0074, lower bound -0.0264, upper bound 0.0412, just below the 0.0415 benchmark. I mark it unresolved but closed because the evidence is not supportive and the near-boundary upper limit is too fragile to justify rejection or follow-up. Overall, these results do not establish a coherent cross-outcome feature_063 effect; only the outcome_014 contrast H114 remains plausible.\n\nFeature_057 exact-value contrasts: H228 (outcome_014), H229 (outcome_008), and H230 (outcome_011) compare value 10 with value 5. H228 has signed estimate -0.0055 with interval about -0.0444 to 0.0333; it does not support the claimed direction, but because the upper bound exceeds the outcome_014 benchmark, it remains inconclusive. H229 has signed estimate -0.0116 and upper bound 0.0137, below the outcome_008 benchmark, and is rejected. H230 has signed estimate 0.0154 and interval about -0.0128 to 0.0436; the point estimate is below the outcome_011 benchmark, so it is unresolved but not supportive. The feature_057 line does not show a clinically interval-supported association and is closed.\n\nFeature_048 level contrasts: H231, H232, and H233 compare feature_048 level_001 with level_003 on outcome_008, outcome_011, and outcome_013, with the claimed direction corresponding to lower values in level_001. The signed estimates are 0.0165, 0.0193, and 0.0140, respectively. All point estimates are below their outcome benchmarks and their lower bounds are negative, although the upper bounds still extend into clinically meaningful positive territory. This is not enough to accept, but it is also not enough to rule out a clinically meaningful positive association. I mark all three unresolved and closed as an investigation: there is no coherent evidence of a strong clinically meaningful feature_048 effect, and additional follow-up would not be efficient.\n\nOther categorical explorers: H234 (outcome_014 feature_055 level_001 versus level_002) and H237 (outcome_014 feature_019 level_002 versus level_001) are both inconclusive. H234 has a tiny positive signed estimate 0.0023 with interval about -0.0418 to 0.0463; H237 has signed estimate -0.0114 with interval about -0.0503 to 0.0274. Neither supports the claimed direction, and neither rules out clinically meaningful positive effects under the outcome_014 benchmark. They are unresolved but closed. There are no new clinically interval-supported discoveries in this batch.\n\nCritical review: The main methodological concerns remain multiplicity and post-selection optimism. This run has evaluated many predictor-outcome contrasts, and the 95% discovery intervals are not adjusted for that search. The feature_063 contrast H114 remains the only candidate with a zero-excluding interval and a point estimate well above benchmark. However, its lower bound is below the benchmark, the outcome_014 mean is relatively small so the 10%-of-mean benchmark is somewhat lenient in absolute terms, and the effect is only about 0.10 outcome_014 SD, which is modest. The new coherence evidence is mixed: the level_003-versus-level_002 result is supportive but imprecise, while cross-outcome feature_063 contrasts are null or boundary failures. I therefore do not accept H114 from discovery evidence alone. I request independent validation of H114 as the only central candidate. If validation raises the combined or independent evidence to a clinically interval-supported level, H114 could be accepted as a dataset-specific association; if validation is null or non-clinical, the feature_063 line should be closed. These remain associations in the supplied dataset, not causal or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 14 appraise state: accepted supported associations remain empty. Prior validations have closed most early positive lines, including feature_042-outcome_001 and feature_032-outcome_014 subgroup signals. Current clinical-support rule: signed 95% lower bound >= about 0.10*absolute outcome mean. Benchmarks: outcome_014 0.0093; outcome_013 0.0269; outcome_011 0.0301; outcome_008 0.0282; outcome_001 0.0415. New evidence: feature_063 coherence across outcomes is weak. H227 outcome_014 level_003 vs level_002 is positive but wide; H133 outcome_013 rejected; H222 outcome_011 rejected; H134 outcome_001 near-boundary unresolved. Only H114 (outcome_014 feature_063 level_002 vs level_001, signed estimate 0.036, interval 0.002 to 0.070) remains active. Feature_057 contrasts are unsupported or inconclusive; feature_048 contrasts are weakly positive but below benchmark and closed; feature_055/019 contrasts are closed inconclusive. No claim accepted from this batch. Validation requested for H114 because it is the closest plausible clinical candidate and the best use of the remaining validation budget. If validation is non-clinical or contradicts discovery, close H114 and feature_063. If validation confirms with clinically meaningful interval support, accept H114 as dataset-specific association and consider H141 dose-response follow-up only if needed. Closed or low-priority predictor families: feature_042, feature_054, feature_002, feature_034, feature_060, feature_048, feature_057, feature_055, feature_019, feature_032, feature_065, and most feature_045 evidence. Remaining broad exploration may target untested predictors with adequate cell counts, especially feature_009 and other common categorical predictors, but only after H114 validation is assessed. Maintain critical caveats: many comparisons, unadjusted false-positive risk, post-selection subgroup risks, absolute-mean benchmark may be lenient for outcome_014, and all conclusions are dataset-specific associations.",
